7|0@Israel^1440507030#cuezwsm:RdMrcr$:I think it's funny that Israel is seen as a role model for it's military, the Israeli model is terrible. You are literally a slave of the state, you are being forced to work without your consent. To add insult to injury, you get 550-1100 NIS per month (140$-280$), now consider the fact that it is more expensive to live in Israel than to live in most of western Europe, so you're not even compensated fairly for your slavery. The service is extremely long compared to other countries, 24 months for girls and 32 for boys. It is a huge money drain, the military budget is huge - but also growing very fast. Any soldier has personal experiences of how inefficiently (to say the least) money is being spent. Conscription is by absolutely no means necessary for our defense, what the state is trying to sell us is that we need conscription because that's the only way to bring people of different backgrounds together, which is why most of our military is a summer camp - people serving just for the sake of serving, sitting all day long counting the days. Our military even has a radio station, hospital clowns, magicians (although those are novelties, the huge part is simply people who have nothing to do). Very little to do with defense, a lot to do with social engineering. While the rhetoric may be that serving is important, Israelis have an unhealthy jealousy for people who are exempt from service (like Arabs and ultra-Orthodox), and many soldiers would get out if they only could.
